      "question_id": "Q7",
      "question": "How does the ingestion worker process documents and what database does it use?",
      "category": "complex",
      "result": {
        "answer": "The ingestion worker processes documents by polling Redis streams for new ingestion jobs, then processing them asynchronously using a JobProcessor. It coordinates the entire ingestion pipeline from Git \u2192 Database \u2192 ChromaDB.\n\nAccording to the documentation, the ingestion worker uses PostgreSQL as its database for storing documents, and ChromaDB for storing embeddings.",
